    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d812">

                <pb facs="1276" n="1262" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1262"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 European War/11–744: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Chargé to the Czechoslovak Government in Exile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Schoenfeld</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">at London</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-14T20:00:00-04:00">November 14,
                            1944—8 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8. The Department will issue a warning to German authorities<anchor n="56"
                        xml:id="d812-f1"/> in line with your Zecho 22, November 7, 7 p.m., on
                    November 15. OWI publicity will be arranged. British Embassy here expects BBC to
                    publicize similar British warning at about the same time.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d812-f1" n="56" xml:id="d812-f1-content">
                <p>For text of warning, see <hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, November 19, 1944,
                    p. 596.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
